  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "Why. The shipped captain's board drifted from the prototype the captain approved on 2026-10-07, because the prototype was turned into prose and nobody compared the rendered pages with it. Code review checks logic, not layout (captain rule, 2026-10-11: a designer with a fresh context reviews every change that touches pages).",
    "What, designer round. A designer round is a reviewer-role round with its own skill file, `skills/designer/SKILL.md`: the same launcher, sandbox, crew policy and signed evidence as the code reviewer, a fresh context each time, and a vendor and model set in config that default to the reviewer's.",
    "What, designer skill. `skills/designer/SKILL.md` is written in our own words from these sources at these commits: pbakaus/impeccable@d631a8827f99414d2b6daba4ef08b7f8701751d7 (Apache-2.0), OneRedOak/claude-code-workflows@29a34c725313c7621f426f838ed31cf482473fb4 (MIT), vercel-labs/web-interface-guidelines@434b7f91364665f2f733b310ec54809bf8f37937 (MIT), ehmo/platform-design-skills@dc2be825d8b439caea78e9eaa8fb3ac23b0ff3e9 (MIT), nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill@67803eac81607188194aea9842a723b89326d90d (MIT) and anthropics/skills@dbd4588f9e1033efb41dad4bef2f7947c8993d44 (skills/frontend-design, Apache-2.0); its header names each source, license and commit, and `skills/designer/NOTICE` carries every source's license notice.",
    "What, UI paths. A pull request is a UI change when its diff touches a path that matches the project's `ui` globs; the defaults cover page files (`**/*.html`, `**/*.css`, `**/*.scss`, `**/*.tsx`, `**/*.jsx`, `**/*.vue`, `**/*.svelte`), and this repository's config sets its `ui` to the defaults plus `board/public/**`. A pull request that is not a UI change runs no designer round and merges exactly as today.",
    "What, capture. Before the designer runs, every page the pull request changes is captured at web widths 320, 390, 768, 1440 and 1920 plus each CSS breakpoint edge, in light and dark (apps: small phone, large phone and tablet, portrait and landscape), both for the pull request head and, when the task's spec names a prototype in `design.prototype` (a folder under `state/prototypes/`), for that prototype. If any capture fails, the round does not start.",
    "What, verdict. The designer compares the pages one by one and ends with APPROVE or REJECT. Each finding names the page, the viewport, the problem and a fix: a diff, or a pointer to the part of the prototype to follow. Findings use the code reviewer's format. Without a prototype the designer reviews with the general design rules in its skill.",
    "What, parallel. On the same head the design review runs at the same time as the code review; the autopilot starts whichever of the two is missing without waking firstmate.",
    "What, gate. The merge gate needs the design APPROVE, bound to the same head, only for a UI change; a design REJECT goes to the worker like any review finding and counts toward the review round budget.",
    "What, prototype check. One command runs the same designer round on a prototype folder, so firstmate can have a prototype reviewed before the captain sees it; the result is recorded and gates nothing.",
    "What, merge card. The merge card of a UI change shows each page's prototype and result screenshots side by side behind a toggle.",
    "What, round reads. A Claude round can read its own `pinned/` folder and its local-tests folder, which the OS sandbox already allows; today the Claude adapter's own deny rules hide them, so a worker cannot read the pinned spec and design its prompt points to. A designer round can also read, read-only, the one prototype folder its task names in `design.prototype`, so a REJECT can point to the prototype's HTML and CSS. No round can read another round's folders or any other part of `state/`.",
    "Docs. `skills/firstmate/SKILL.md`, `skills/reviewer/SKILL.md` and its rule inventory entries, and `design/design.md` (the crew roles and the merge gates) describe the designer round, and `.github/workflows/ci.yml` installs the browser the capture needs.",
    "Done, tests. New tests prove: a non-UI pull request merges with no designer round (`design: non-ui pr unaffected`, regression); a UI pull request is held at the merge gate until a design APPROVE on its head exists (`design: ui pr needs approve`, fail-first); a failed capture starts no round (`design: capture failure blocks`, fail-first); a REJECT reaches the worker and counts a round (`design: reject counts a round`, fail-first); the autopilot starts the missing design round (`design: missing round started`, fail-first); the project's `ui` globs replace the defaults (`design: project ui globs used`, fail-first); the skill header lists every source with license and commit and NOTICE exists (`design: skill sources recorded`, fail-first).",
    "Done, reads. Tests show a Claude round reads its own pinned file (`adapter: own pinned readable`, fail-first), cannot read another round's pinned file (`adapter: other pinned hidden`), and a designer round reads its task's prototype folder but no other prototype (`design: prototype readable`)."
  ],
